  "corrections_after_the_fact": [
    "gpt-5.6-luna was first scored 6/7 on 'separates static validation from measured efficiency'. Its text reads 'use tokens.py for static layer/load diagnostics, but treat size only as a diagnostic. Use bench.py for the authorized A/B'. The check required the word 'benchmark'. Fixed in grade.py and re-graded across every stored output of the day: all Claude, Codex and Hermes verdicts unchanged except luna; claude-haiku-4-5 still fails the check.",
    "Before this round, runtimes.py summed Codex's cached_input_tokens on top of input_tokens. OpenAI's input_tokens already includes the cached part, so context and cost would have been overstated. Fixed before the round ran: input_tokens is normalized to the fresh part on every runtime, and cached tokens are priced at the cached rate."
  ],
  "findings": [
    "All four Codex models passed every objective expectation; all four opened references/refactoring.md, evaluation.md and runtimes.md (4 to 6 reads each), which the review contract points at.",
    "API-equivalent cost spans 44x within one runtime for the same verdict: luna US$ 0.0075, terra 0.072, sol 0.136, astra 0.332.",
